FTXUI 7.0.3 writes the whole screen on every frame and reads input 128 bytes at
a time, so one key costs ~3 KiB on the terminal and queued keys need many frames.
App has no output hook, so noteapp (T75) adds the smallest one:
- App::SetFrameWriter: noteapp's src/tui/frame_diff.cpp writes changed cells only.
- FetchTerminalEvents: 4096-byte read, all queued input lands in one frame.
Drop this patch when upstream offers an output hook; re-check at every FTXUI bump.

